  "verbalization": "Tetracycline appears to be linked to Yaws through a shared pathway involving Sulfisoxazole, which is indicated in multiple conditions. The evidence suggests that Tetracycline may act as a potential repurposed drug for Yaws, as it is associated with the same intermediate (Sulfisoxazole) in three distinct indications—Cat-scratch Disease, Ornithosis, and Chancroid—each of which is linked to Yaws. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the strength varies slightly across the three paths. The mechanism appears to involve the use of Sulfisoxazole as a bridge between Tetracycline and Yaws, though the exact mode of action remains unclear. The presence of a common intermediate in multiple disease pathways supports the hypothesis that Tetracycline could be a candidate for repurposing in Yaws, provided further mechanistic validation is conducted.",
